UID:omsi-20261114T110000-running-wild-return-to-the-river-2026@small-screen
 s-pdx
DTSTAMP:20261104T202843Z
DTSTART:20261114T190000Z
DTEND:20261114T194500Z
SUMMARY:Running Wild: Return to the River (2026)
LOCATION:OMSI Empirical Theatre\, 1945 SE Water Ave\, Portland OR
GEO:45.5083;-122.6672
DESCRIPTION:Dir. Myles Connolly · 45 min\n\nPacific salmon swim upstream o
 n their homeward journey\, bearing witness to the interconnected web of li
 fe linking land and sea.\n\nTickets: https://tickets.omsi.edu/events/019e4
 239-a7c0-1590-2d4f-a3686e412dc4\n\nMore showtimes: https://mattlohkamp.git
 hub.io/small-screens-pdx/
URL:https://tickets.omsi.edu/events/019e4239-a7c0-1590-2d4f-a3686e412dc4
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:omsi-20261114T120000-shark-kingdom-2025@small-screens-pdx
DTSTAMP:20261107T001903Z
DTSTART:20261114T200000Z
DTEND:20261114T204000Z
SUMMARY:Shark Kingdom (2025)
LOCATION:OMSI Empirical Theatre\, 1945 SE Water Ave\, Portland OR
GEO:45.5083;-122.6672
DESCRIPTION:Dir. Dave Duce · 40 min\n\nShark heroes and conservationists J
 ess Cramp\, Liv Rose and Cristina Zenato lead this epic family adventure i
 nto the kingdom of sharks\, where we’ll come face to face with these anc
 ient and awe-inspiring animals and learn how our future is intertwined wit
 h theirs.  Each shark species wields unique powers that help them survive 
 in diverse ecosystems\, whether it’s a great white hunting in the wild a
 nd wind-swept seas of New Zealand\, whaler sharks learning to coexist with
  Australian fishermen\, or elusive oceanic white tip “shipwreck sharks
 ” traversing uncharted depths of the Pacific.  In some of the world’s 
 most beautiful diving locations\, join the action to understand and help t
 hese magnificent creatures\, and be immersed in the larger story of our sh
 ared oceans.\n\nTickets: https://tickets.omsi.edu/events/019987c5-cb0c-bec
 3-97a1-13641c5b3233\n\nMore showtimes: https://mattlohkamp.github.io/small
 -screens-pdx/
URL:https://tickets.omsi.edu/events/019987c5-cb0c-bec3-97a1-13641c5b3233
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:omsi-20261114T123000-space-the-new-frontier-2024@small-screens-pdx
DTSTAMP:20261107T001903Z
DTSTART:20261114T203000Z
DTEND:20261114T211500Z
SUMMARY:Space: The New Frontier (2024)
LOCATION:OMSI Empirical Theatre\, 1945 SE Water Ave\, Portland OR
GEO:45.5083;-122.6672
DESCRIPTION:Dir. Jake Flannery · 45 min\n\nA second golden age of space ha
 s quietly dawned on us\, with new hope for humanity as a spacefaring speci
 es. Space: The New Frontier\, a new documentary made for Giant Screen thea
 ters\, goes behind the scenes of some of the most promising space technolo
 gies and missions of our time\, giving audiences a first look into the not
 -so-distant future.\n\nTickets: https://tickets.omsi.edu/events/019783f8-5
 c3e-818c-8db2-9b1c0d1feaaa\n\nMore showtimes: https://mattlohkamp.github.i
 o/small-screens-pdx/
URL:https://tickets.omsi.edu/events/019783f8-5c3e-818c-8db2-9b1c0d1feaaa
END:VEVENT
